[TEXT] **Found the root cause.** Router6's iptables FORWARD chain has an ACL on `eth2` (WAN interface, 10.50.1.2/24) that:
1. **ACCEPTs** only TCP from 172.16.10.0/24 → 172.18.51.1:80
2. **DROPs all other TCP** entering from eth2
3. **DROPs all other UDP** entering from eth2
4. **DROPs all other protocols (including ICMP)** entering from eth2 — 30 packets already counted

Router6 itself can still ping outbound (FORWARD chain doesn't apply to locally-originated traffic, only transit). This is an ACL fault. Entering the skill to complete the structured confirmation:
